nAcademics\nDoctoral Studies and Alumni activities\nDoctoral Studies\nIn-person drop-offs are possible Tuesdays, 9 - 11 a.m., and Thursdays, 9 - 11 a.m. and 13 - 15 p.m.\nPlease direct inquiries by e-mail to doctoral-studies@fb5.rwth-aachen.de.\nDoctoral Studies\nAdmission Requirements\nInitiation of Process\nOrganization of the oral doctoral examination\nOral Examination\nSubmission of Obligatory Copies\nBasic Information\nTo become familiar with the doctoral process at the Faculty of Georesources and Materials Engineering you can refer to the current Doctoral Regulation (as of August 1, 2025 - at the moment only available in German; the English former version of the Doctoral Regulation (not in force any more)). Here you find a schematic presentation of the procedure.\nIn the Code for Doctoral Studies, RWTH commits itself to principles and standards for the design of the doctoral process. These guidelines help to ensure the quality of doctoral qualification and form the basis for its continuous development. During conflicts, the Academic Ombudsperson is available to doctoral students as a point of contact.\nContact Persons for Doctoral Studies\nDr. Kristina Fischer (dt./engl.) Tel.: 0241-80-97214\nSabine Quaedflieg Tel.: 0241-80-97214 (outside office hours the phone number is not available)\nEmail: promotionen@fb5.rwth-aachen.de\nAddress:\nFaculty of Georesources and Materials Engineering of RWTH Aachen University\nOffice for Postgraduate Study\nIntzestr. 1, 52072 Aachen,\n1st floor, right, Room 100.0\nFooter\nRWTH\nRWTH Main Page\nContacts and Maps\nMaps and Accessibility\nMaps - Buildings\nInstitutions\nDean's Office\nServices\nJob Openings\nContact\nLegal Notice\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nSitemap\n\u00a9 2026 RWTH Aachen University", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://www.fb5.rwth-aachen.de/cms/georessourcen/studium/promotion/~bcpd/ablauf-einer-promotion/?lidx=1#main"], ["Skip to Main Navigation", "https://www.fb5.rwth-aachen.de/cms/georessour